---
/**
 * The whole way from a fresh server to a first environment, in its real
 * order, the step in the dashboard included: `spawner up` stops on a
 * project an admin has not added yet.
 */
import { docsSource, isRelease } from '../../lib/docs-source';
import { INSTALL_COMMAND } from '../../lib/site';
import CopyCommand from './CopyCommand.astro';

const source = docsSource();
---

<section class="section" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="section-title" id="install-title">Install it on your server</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">
      Four steps from a fresh server to a first environment. The server: Ubuntu 22.04 or 24.04, or Debian 12, amd64 or arm64, 4&nbsp;GiB of memory
      at least (8&nbsp;GiB or more advised), ports 80 and 443.
    </p>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <h3>Set up the server</h3>
        <p>
          On a Linux server dedicated to previews, with a DNS record such as <code>*.preview.example.com</code> pointing to it. The installer asks
          for the domain, an e-mail and your DNS provider, sets up Docker, and prints the link that creates the first admin account.
        </p>
        <CopyCommand command={INSTALL_COMMAND} label="the install command" />
        <p class="aside">
          <a href="/docs/install/#reading-the-installer-first">Read the script before running it</a>, or
          <a href="/docs/install/#a-local-install">try Spawner in a local VM</a>, without a domain.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Install the CLI and log in</h3>
        <p>
          On your machine, with Node.js 20 or later. Then run <code>spawner login</code> with the dashboard’s address,
          <code>spawner.preview.example.com</code> for that domain: it opens the dashboard, where you enter the code it shows.
        </p>
        <CopyCommand command="npm install -g spawner-cli" label="the command that installs the CLI" />
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Add the project</h3>
        <p>
          In the dashboard, an admin opens <strong>Projects</strong>, then <strong>New project</strong>: a slug, the repository, and for a monorepo
          the directory that holds <code>.spawner/</code>.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Start its first environment</h3>
        <p>
          In the project: <code>init</code> writes <code>.spawner/</code> (add <code>--project</code> with the slug if it is not the directory’s
          name), <code>up</code> starts the environment of the branch.
        </p>
        <CopyCommand command="spawner init && spawner up --wait" label="the command that starts a first environment" />
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="more">
      <a href="/docs/quickstart/">The quickstart</a> goes through each step.
      {
        isRelease(source) && (
          <>
            The latest release is Spawner {source.version}: <a href="/changelog/">what changed</a>.
          </>
        )
      }
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .steps {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2rem;
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: step;
  }

  li {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    padding-left: 3rem;
    counter-increment: step;
  }

  li::before {
    content: counter(step);
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--sp-accent-border);
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--sp-accent-soft);
    color: var(--sp-accent-text);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  h3 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 2rem;
  }

  li p {
    color: var(--sp-text-2);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  li strong {
    color: var(--sp-text);
  }

  .aside {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  .more {
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin-top: 2.25rem;
    color: var(--sp-text-2);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 30rem) {
    li {
      padding-left: 0;
    }

    h3 {
      padding-left: 2.75rem;
    }
  }
</style>
